-- title:
--   Extracting a completed-zeta zero list from a band certificate
-- statement:
--   Let $a,b$ be real and $K$ a nonnegative integer. If a band certificate supplies
--   $K$ strictly increasing ordinates in $(a,b)$ at which zeta and completed zeta
--   both vanish on the critical line, then there are real numbers
--   $t_1<\cdots<t_K$ such that
--
--   $$a\le t_j\le b,\qquad \Lambda(1/2+it_j)=0\quad(1\le j\le K),$$
--
--   where $\Lambda$ is the completed Riemann zeta function. The empty list is allowed
--   when $K=0$.
--
--   This is the zero-list interface consumed by the subsequent zero-count argument.
-- source:
--   https://github.com/DrMurphyIsIn/Arda/blob/af4fde8972eb6d4e78c7d9a95933b18b81adf52d/telperion/examples/zeta_reflection/lean/RS5_Band.lean#L256-L262

